Description: CVE-2026-56373 - fix use-after-free in PDB reader comment path
 In coders/pdb.c ReadPDBImage(), when the ResizeQuantumMemory realloc for the
 comment buffer fails, the code writes the NUL terminator (*r='\0') through
 the now-stale pointer before checking whether the allocation succeeded.
 Move the NULL check ahead of the NUL-terminator write so the terminator is
 only written to a still-valid buffer.
 .
 Advisory: GHSA-3j4x-rwrx-xxj9
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/168ffe18def968f886c023146a478897866fd621
Author: Dirk Lemstra <dirk@lemstra.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-11
---
--- a/coders/pdb.c
+++ b/coders/pdb.c
@@ -624,9 +624,9 @@
         *r=c;
         c=ReadBlobByte(image);
       }
-      *r='\0';
       if (comment == (char *) NULL)
         ThrowReaderException(ResourceLimitError,"MemoryAllocationFailed");
+      *r='\0';
       (void) SetImageProperty(image,"comment",comment,exception);
       comment=DestroyString(comment);
     }
Description: CVE-2026-66011 - Fix memory leak in magick CLI on invalid options
 InterpretImageProperties() in MagickCore/property.c leaked the interpreted
 text buffer, the cloned property image and property ImageInfo on several
 early-error/allocation-failure paths (empty "%[]" escape, unbalanced braces,
 ResizeQuantumMemory/AcquireString failures). The MagickWand CLI command
 handler CLINoImageOperator() in MagickWand/operation.c leaked previously
 interpreted arg1/arg2 strings when re-interpreting them for the "set" and
 "clone" operators. In addition, the ImageInfo cloned inside the DrawInfo by
 AcquireMagickCLI()/CloneDrawInfo() was never released, leaking on every
 magick CLI invocation, including when invalid options abort processing.
 .
 This backport consolidates the InterpretImageProperties cleanup onto a single
 "cleanup:" goto label driving a status flag, frees the stale interpreted
 argument strings before re-interpreting them in the CLI operator, and frees
 the DrawInfo-embedded ImageInfo both at acquisition (wandcli.c) and at CLI
 teardown (magick-cli.c). Purely cosmetic upstream churn (comment removal,
 whitespace, variable-declaration restyling) is intentionally omitted to keep
 the backport minimal; the fx/hex/pixel local "status" variables are renamed
 to "fx_status" only to avoid shadowing the newly introduced function-level
 status flag.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/e3e69118c29064e2716ca89aab635ea95a15dd49
