Description: CVE-2026-61868 - Fix memory leak of chroma_image in ReadYUVImage error paths
 The YUV decoder (ReadYUVImage) allocates chroma_image via CloneImage inside
 the read loop, but several error paths that trigger when a subsequent
 OpenBlob() call fails (PartitionInterlace Y/U/V component files) return
 without releasing chroma_image, causing a memory leak (CWE-401).
 This backport adds the missing chroma_image=DestroyImage(chroma_image) calls
 to those error paths. The remaining changes in the upstream commit are purely
 cosmetic (local-variable reordering and whitespace) and are omitted.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/808506dc4d0cbf3972ce0d57544a06209b65009c
